    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The largest Mississippian centre, built from about 1050 on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> floodplain opposite present-day St Louis.</li><li>Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monks-mound">Monks Mound</a>, about 30 metres high, is the largest prehistoric earthwork in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>.</li><li>From the late 12th century the city shrank behind a palisade, and by about 1350 it was largely abandoned.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>From the centre of Cahokia’s reconstructed Woodhenge, a circle of 48 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timber">timber</a> posts, the sun rises over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monks-mound">Monks Mound</a> at the spring and autumn equinoxes.</p></aside>
    </section>

